      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Exclusive: Telegram urged to clarify how it detects illegal incitement after attacks were coordinated using app</p><p>Telegram is facing questions from Ofcom over how it detects and prevents illegal incitement after a Ukrainian man was found guilty of carrying out arson attacks on a car and property associated with Keir Starmer.</p><p>A spokesperson for the regulator said it had contacted the messaging app “to seek further clarification” because the arsonist had been directed on Telegram <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jun/15/two-men-found-guilty-over-arson-attacks-linked-to-keir-starmer\">by a handler linked to Russia</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jun/19/telegram-ofcom-arsonist-starmer-linked-properties\">Continue reading...</a>"
